# Repair result

All three retained generator findings are repaired for the requested easy band.

- **Fidelity:** nine source matrices and complete answer banks/fields replay. q-139629 now restores the independently supported (3,1) highlight and retains the source field order and solution; all sixteen cells of its observed 4x4 family are tested.
- **Correctness and grading:** visible matrix coordinates independently determine keys and solutions. Indexed symbolic blanks are available in ordinary practice. Generic native indexed-symbol parsing accepts valid braces/labels and rejects different indices, bases and numeric entry values. Engine patch, exact rebuild commands, unit results and strict native reports are under evidence/.
- **Decision variation:** answer-bearing roles move within whole observed banks. Finite radio groups contain distinct highlighted targets. Controlled banks cover all five choice roles/positions, and incidental entry changes preserve answers. The retained bank-only cue is no longer reliable; delivery filtering preserves the tested target sets. The prospective five-record batch has no item of the reported shape, so that fact alone is not used as proof; explicit current CLI profile batches and controlled records test it non-vacuously.
- **Packaging/rendering:** exact dependencies, relocated replay and invalid inputs pass. Four representative UI cases and a final corrected 4x4 screenshot were inspected. No generated image assets are needed.

Reproduce with `.venv/bin/python -B <workspace>/check_repair.py --check source`, `--check shortcut`, or `--check grading` from the repository. The scripts resolve current runtime files and invoke the shared delivery filter/native grader; they never mutate runtime code or database content. `check_package.py` retains the relocation and small-sample validation. `evidence/commands-*.json` contains exact argument arrays and results.

Limits: validation targets easy; inherited authored moderate/hard extensions were not independently certified in this repair. Learner-specific history and live database selection were unavailable; the captured inventory and actual shared publication filter were inspected read-only. No proven eligible stored generated defect was found. Runtime source-replay requests preserve literal source arrangements and are not a shortcut-resistant practice pool by themselves.
pub fn select(
    s: &EntitySnapshot,
    candidates: &[u64],
    distribution: Option<[f64; 3]>,
    seed: &str,
) -> Result<Option<u64>> {
    let candidates: Vec<_> = candidates
        .iter()
        .copied()
        .collect::<BTreeSet<_>>()
        .into_iter()
        .collect();
    // Preserve old, unconfigured policies; the default policy supplies weights.
    let Some(distribution) = distribution else {
        return Ok(candidates.first().copied());
    };
    if distribution.iter().any(|w| !w.is_finite() || *w < 0.0)
        || !distribution.iter().sum::<f64>().is_finite()
        || distribution.iter().sum::<f64>() <= 0.0
    {
        return Err("invalid question-weight distribution".into());
    }
    let mut bands: [Vec<u64>; 3] = std::array::from_fn(|_| vec![]);
    let mut unrated = vec![];
    for q in candidates {
        let Some(value) = s
            .entity(q)?
            .get("question/difficulty")
            .filter(|v| !v.is_null())
        else {
            unrated.push(q);
            continue;
        };
        let difficulty = s.ident(value)?;
        let band = BANDS
            .iter()
            .position(|b| difficulty == format!("question.difficulty/{b}"))
            .ok_or("question has an unsupported difficulty enum")?;
        bands[band].push(q);
    }
    let digest = Sha256::digest(format!("course-academy/question-selection/v1/{seed}"));
    let uniform = |offset| {
        let bits = u64::from_be_bytes(digest[offset..offset + 8].try_into().unwrap()) >> 11;
        bits as f64 / (1u64 << 53) as f64
    };
    let total: f64 = distribution
        .iter()
        .enumerate()
        .filter(|(i, _)| !bands[*i].is_empty())
        .map(|(_, w)| *w)
        .sum();
    let pool = if total > 0.0 {
        let mut draw = uniform(0) * total;
        let mut chosen = None;
        for (i, w) in distribution.iter().enumerate() {
            if bands[i].is_empty() || *w == 0.0 {
                continue;
            }
            chosen = Some(i);
            if draw < *w {
                break;
            }
            draw -= *w;
        }
        &bands[chosen.unwrap()]
    } else {
        &unrated
    };
    Ok(if pool.is_empty() {
        None
    } else {
        Some(pool[(uniform(8) * pool.len() as f64) as usize])
    })
}

